## The one permission that is granted: modpacks

You may include Freehold in a modpack, public or private, on any platform, and
you may redistribute the unmodified mod file as part of that pack. No request
is necessary. This permission also covers:

- **Configuration and datapacks.** You may change the starting values, and you
  may write and ship your own goods, building and blueprint definitions
  alongside the mod.

- **Derived assets, if you name where they came from.** Textures, models and
  blueprints that start from ours may be shipped with your pack, provided the
  pack states that they are derived from Freehold. ASSETS-LICENSE.md says
  which files count as assets.

Your own resource packs and your own datapacks do not need this permission at
all: shipping work you made yourself redistributes nothing of ours.

Nothing here grants the right to redistribute the mod outside a modpack, to
publish modified builds of the mod itself, or to use the name Freehold for
another work.

